Wing Commander OCS - enhanced-framerate candidate
Original slave: Psygore. Improvements: Vesa Halttunen.

Enhanced framerate (68020+Fast RAM)

The launch icon enables CUSTOM5=1 and DCACHE by default. DCACHE requests both
instruction and data caches; use NOCACHE to override caching explicitly. Clear this checkbox in WHDLoad,
set CUSTOM5=0, or remove the tooltype to use the original game behaviour:
per-frame simulation, original rendering, frame waits and cache request.

Enhancements only activate on the verified English OCS SPS 1657 game, with a
68020 or better and verified true Fast RAM. A 68000/68010, Chip/slow RAM only, or an unverified memory bank always uses original
behaviour, even with CUSTOM5=1. Values other than 1 also use original behaviour.
Slow expansion RAM does not qualify merely because Exec labels it MEMF_FAST.

Enhanced mode uses a 10 Hz world for flight and the title/asteroid intro,
responsive input and bounded extrapolation between updates. Music and credit
text deadlines remain native. The CPU converter uses verified Fast source
storage; when that allocation is unavailable, conversion safely retains the
native blitter. That conversion fallback does not disable an already selected
10 Hz mode. No 25/50 FPS guarantee follows from enabling the option.

CUSTOM1 (language), CUSTOM2 (cheats), CUSTOM3 (system) and CUSTOM4 (mission)
retain their original meanings. German and other revisions have no enhancement
support. CD32 CUSTOM5 mode numbers do not apply to this OCS slave.
Quit uses the original '*' / PrtSc key unless WHDLoad QUITKEY overrides it.

The public slave adds 64 KiB of native game-pool headroom for cockpit images.
This startup memory reservation applies with the enhancement toggle off too.

Tested launcher floor: 512 KiB Chip + 4 MiB true Fast, including PRELOAD.
The focused 68020/Fast model is the performance target. This is not a full
campaign, arbitrary accelerator/cache or real-hardware compatibility claim.
The measured A500 enhancement experiments were too slow in heavy scenes;
the public candidate therefore always keeps original behaviour on that CPU.
Cold-boot save reload and physical controller acceptance remain release checks.

Original installer and icon credits remain applicable. CPU conversion uses
Kalms' four-plane routines. This is an OCS candidate, separate from the CD32
release and its options. Do not mix the two variants' game assets or slaves.
